{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790431994,"nonce":"m7OKK/N5jeZCvmOg6xFJhLGJNdQ=","message":"Stage 3 first slice landed: c39518f (helper signature table), 5e08774 (ObjInstance aligned to 8: wasm32 fields were misaligned), c966ce4 (uncaught AOT errors exit 70; native AOT had the same silent-exit bug, 46f9dbe), 7c2a0e5 (LLVM AOT).\n\nWhat works: codegen/llvm_aot.rs lowers walked modules into one object for an LlvmTarget (triple, CPU, features; wasm32 defaults to generic + sign-ext, mutable-globals, bulk-memory, nontrapping-fptoint, multivalue, reference-types). The module's triple and data layout, every function's target-cpu/target-features, and the layout table all come from the target, and the object runs through LLVM's default\u003cO3\u003e. The bootstrap installs classes (method descriptors are LLVM structs checked against Layout), closures, cross-module and runtime imports, and on wasm is __main_void. tests/wasm_aot.rs links with rust-lld against wlift_runtime.o and runs under wasmtime: control flow, strings, closures, lists and maps, classes with statics and super, a two-module import, fibers that finish, 200k allocations, the uncaught-error exit, and the target features in the object's target_features section. CI runs it in the Linux LLVM job.\n\nRuntime changes for wasm: compiled bodies are entered through entry(args, n), a wrapper the program emits per closure and method (wasm checks call signatures; native callers pass surplus arguments). A yield or suspend inside compiled code raises when there is no fiber stack.\n\nLeft in stage 3:\n- Speed: AOT call sites all go through wren_call_N. Port the Cranelift AOT CHA (build_cha) for direct and class-dispatched calls, and re-enable the list fast paths the AOT mode skips.\n- Foreign classes and bundled native libraries are refused in an LLVM AOT build.\n- Native LLVM AOT for the host triple works in principle but has no test. Link it with link_executable like tests/aot_runtime.rs.\n- No CLI yet (`wlift --aot out.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1`); stage 5.\n- Fibers that yield in compiled frames: c079735.\n- Roots on wasm (stage 6): a body keeps everything it allocated rooted until it returns (no loop-header release). That is safe for values held in its own locals but grows the root store in long loops. Values passed on to callees are covered only by the callee's own scope.\n\nFound along the way: 2dde65f (System.print and interpolation ignore a user toString), f16f4db (a fiber's first call(v) doesn't bind the parameter). Both are in every mode.","files":null}]}